deo I'll attempt to show this I'll  also include a couple of very basic  builds at the end of the video to get  you started I'm going to go ahead and  assume that you've made it to level 30  and to world tier 5 the same principles  can be used in tier 1 to 4 but in all  honesty if you aren't there yet get to  world tier 5 this is where the game  really begins first step what do you  want to achieve with the build do you  want to be putting up maximum damage  with your guns do you like the idea of  having strong damage dealing skills  would you rather play as a more of a  support bill  within the team or maybe you'd rather  focus on sustainability because you'll  be playing solo most of the time  whatever way you want to go you'll need  to figure this out first you can speak  into multiple different things and this  will be fine for a lot of the easier  content in the game but later on you'll  find you won't be quite strong enough  for do enough damage to be able to make  it through some of the more difficult  content the game has changed over the  years in the direction to promote more  of a role based to play for example the  team consisting of a healer DPS build  skill build and a tank build will have  more success than a team full of solo  player builds this example is probably  oversimplifying it a little bit but  hopefully you get the idea  build synergy and team synergy is the  key so it doesn't miss Sara to start out  with picking your role but it's a good  practice to get into and don't worry  about being stuck in a certain role this  is why we have loadouts  you can save and chop and change between  builds depending on the activity and  what your team requires once you've  decided on the build or roll direction  you'd like to take you can now start  picking through the items you pick up to  find the best gear and weapons to  complement your build so if you are  after a skill power build you should  look out for gear that complements  electronics and skill haste and weapons  that have talents that will further  increase the damage or intensity of your  skills with a DPS build you want your  gear to help with increasing your  firearms and damage output with weapons  that further increase your damage as a  solo player you'll need to be conscious  of your health so stamina and health  replenishment talents are a must I'm not  going to go through every whip and  talent and gear piece that's available  but I'll run through some of the gear  pieces based on the three roles DPS  skill power solo shown on screen right  now are my recommendations as far as the  gear major and minor attributes go for  the purpose of this video I'm showing  gear more suited to the PvE  aspect of the game this is much easier  to understand and a much better place to  start when you don't have all the best  gear in the game in regards to the solo  and DPS builds the major and - stat  options are very similar the main stats  firearms stamina electronics are where  they will differ  set-pieces our gear that offer unique  bonuses based on the number of other  pieces you have equipped from the same  set for example the Nomad set if you  have two pieces of Nomad equipped you  gain 15% health on kill three pieces you  gain an additional constant heal and  with four pieces equipped you gain path  of the Nomad ability these bonuses  particularly when you look at the full  four-piece sets are quite powerful and  offer you the ability to really  specialize in a particular role there  are currently 14 different sets  available each with their own talents  and their own part to play examples of  these are Nomad solo play huge emphasis  on keeping you alive tactician skill  build focuses on max skill power and  getting your skills back quickly  strikers DPS more heads equals more  damage  classified pieces are the same as normal  set pieces but with highest stats and  the ability to grant even greater  bonuses with five and six piece perks  these can be identified by the file icon  located on the top right these can be  used with normal set items but in order  to unlock the five and six piece bonuses  you need all pieces to be classified so  if you had four normal set items and  added a fifth classified item to the  same set  you'll still only have the four piece  bonus unlocked classified items are  currently the most sought-after gear in  the game outside of global events only  the most difficult in-game activities  will award these pieces  gear mods are additional modifications  that you can add to your gear to further  personalize your build there are two  types of gear mods standard gear mods  which increases certain main stat  firearms stamina electronics and also  provide a bonus stat and performance  mods which gives you another bonus stat  your gear can have five standard gear  mods and four performance mods on your  build screen you can see what gear  pieces can take which mods based on  these slots at the bottom left for  standard mods and bottom right for  performance mods  exotic items are rare pieces of gear  that are most sought after much like the  classified gear they are the equivalent  of legendary or artifact items in other  games exotics are known for the unique  exclusive talents they have some are  good some are not  regardless hold on to them quite often  these items are reviewed and an upcoming  patch can see these go from trashed here  to one of the most sought-after items in  the game  regardless of whether you're running a  skill build or a DPS build skills have a  large part to play like everything else  with the covered up until now you need  to pick skills that compliment your  build damage-dealing skills won't do  anything for you if you aren't running  high enough skill power so a DPS or  solar build should focus more on skills  like the pulse and first aid that will  help the damage and survivability skill  power builds this is where you shine you  can run things like support station and  smart cover if you'd like to support the  team or you can push out some extra  damage using skills like seeker Minds  sticky bomb or turret talents add small  bonuses that can really make or break  certain situations some are quite  specific with what will they give and  can really make a difference depending  on what you're running as a rough guide  some of the more commonly used talents  are critical save combat medic strike  back precision on the move and one is  none  have you found the perfect weapon but it  has a talent that just doesn't work for  you or maybe you have a good nomad piece  that dropped with electronics but you  really needed firearms no problem this  is where the recalibration station comes  in all weapons and gear can have a  single perk or attribute re rolled into  something different you can do this as  many times as you want the gear it cost  standard credits and weapons it cost  Phoenix credits and weapon kits the only  exception is the classified gear this  can have two perks re-rolled  every item excluding mods has a gear  score the gear score is an indication of  how optimized the gear piece or weapon  is your character is then given a gear  score based on the average of all of  your weapons and gear this isn't an  indication of the type of gear or weapon  and has nothing to do with the talents  for example if I had two lightweight M  force and one had damage rating of 18  point 4 K and the other had a rating of  18 point 2 K the one with a higher  damage would have a higher gear score  but does that make it a bit of weapon if  the 18 point 2 K has better talents this  is still a better gun to use and the  same goes for gear a new player can be  forgiven for thinking that the higher  the gear score the bit of the item is  this isn't necessarily untrue but if the  talents are worse and you end up  breaking set bonuses stick with the low  gear score items I've seen a number of  285 plus gear score builds that are much  less effective than some 260 gear score  builds repeating myself again it's all  about synergy between the weapons  talents and gear pieces at almost two  years old I'm not sure how useful this  video will be but I love this game and  if I can help keep the player base  growing I'm more than happy to keep  producing content like this new players  let me know if I can provide more  clarity and I'll do my best either  through the comments section or future  videos day 1 or longtime players of the  game let me know if missed anything  vital as I said earlier this is just  meant to be a simplified version of how  to create a build there is a huge number  of options that I haven't discussed here  but on requests I'll be happy to go into  more detail on screen should be some  very basic DPS skill and solo builds  that can be used as a starting point  take a screenshot but they should be  taken as just that a starting point  modify and adapt these to your style of  play anyway as always thank you very  much for watching and see you in the  next video Cheers  [Music]
 

